  "worked_solution": "Let $p(t)$ be the rate of change of the population. According to the given information,\n\n$$\np(t)={{6+2t}_{\u23df}}_{\\text{population increase}}-{{(2+0.5t)}_{\u23df}}_{\\text{population decrease}}=4+1.5t.\n$$\n\nLet $P(T)$ represent the population of wolves $T$ years after $2010.$ By the accumulation of change formula, we have\n\n$$\nP(T)=P(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{T}p(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known information and carrying out the necessary integration gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(T) & =P(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{T}p(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =250+{\\int }_{0}^{T}(4+1.5t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =250+(4t+\\frac{3}{4}{t}^{2}){|}_{0}^{T} \\\\  & =250+4T+\\frac{3}{4}{T}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's rewrite our final answer in terms of the original variable  $t.$ We get \n\n$$\nP(t)=250+\\frac{3}{4}{t}^{2}+4t.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
